%T A400429 1828,1772,546,62,2,1828,5968,3516,810,74,2,13820,15818,6480,1170,88,
%U A400429 2,13820,49566,35230,10948,1610,102,2,110954,143610,72174,17808,2180,118,2,110954,427580,349822,135092,27434,2856,134,2
%N A400429 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of semi-meanders with n crossings and winding number 2*(k-1) + (n mod 2), for n >= 2, 1 <= k <= floor(n/2).
%C A400429 A semi-meander is a semi-infinite, self-avoiding, directed curve that crosses a line one or more times.
%C A400429 The winding number of a semi-meander is the hypothetical minimum number of self-crossings that would be created if a ray were to start at the source of the semi-infinite directed curve and extend to infinity without crossing the line.
%C A400429 A semi-meander that crosses a line n times, where n is an even number, has an even winding number, 0,2,...,n-2 correspond to k = 1,2,...,floor(n/2). Similarly, if n is odd, then it has an odd winding number, 1,3,...,n-2 correspond to k = 1,2,...,floor(n/2).
%C A400429 Equivalent to a closed curve (a loop) transversely crossing a ray, considered up to continuous deformation fixing the ray, with a winding number equal to the number of crossings that would be created if the fixed end of the ray were extended to form a line.
%C A400429 Analogized to a river (a semi-meander, meander, or loop) crossing a road (a ray, line, or line segment).
%C A400429 Equivalent to a line with vertices, 1,...,2*n, and each vertex, i, joined by an arch below the line to vertex 2*n+1-i for 1 <= i <= n. T(n,k) counts loops that are the union of noncrossing perfect matchings of lower arches with 2*(k-1) + (n mod 2) upper arches that join a vertex <= n to a vertex > n.
%C A400429 Equivalent to a strip of n stamps, folded such that the first stamp is in the first position, also described as leaf 1 on top or as stamp 1 on the outside.
%C A400429 The number of k values in row n equals floor(n/2).
%H A400429 Hunter Hogan, <a href="/A400429/b400429.txt">Table of i, a(i) for i = 2..507</a>
%H A400429 P. Di Francesco, O. Golinelli and E. Guitter, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607039">Meanders: A Direct Enumeration Approach</a>, arXiv:hep-th/9607039, 1996.
